color:rgb(38,40,42);color:rgb(38,40,42);font-family:Helvetica;\"><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></span><br /><div><span style=\"font-size:13.28px;\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\">International Relations and Diplomacy around Today's Global Issues:</span></span></span><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"> &nbsp;Peace and Security, Climate Change, Global Health, Global Migration/ </span></span><span style=\"font-size:13.28px;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\">Displacement,&nbsp;</span></span></span><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"> Human Rights, Poverty/Development, Global Trade, Cyber-Security and the Threat of Artificial Intelligence, etc.)</span></span></span></div>", "<span style=\"font-size:13.28px;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\">Additional information will be provided to the students during the course; maximum 1-2 hours of work outside class. &nbsp;</span></span></span>"], "第14回": ["<span style=\"font-size:13.28px;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\">【Flex Hours 2】</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:13.28px;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\">On-demand format&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"font-size:13.28px;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\">《90 minutes》</span></span></span><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"> (30 min. pre-recorded lecture/presentation; 60 min. homework/self-study) - this can be completed any time from&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"font-size:13.28px;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\">December</span></span></span><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"> &nbsp;11 to&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"font-size:13.28px;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\">December</span></span></span><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"> &nbsp;17</span></span></span><div><span style=\"font-size:13.28px;\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\">Japan's International Cooperation on Selected Global Issues:</span></span></span><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"> &nbsp;Japan and the United Nations, Japan's international development cooperation, Japan's assistance to humanitarian crises and displacement situations, Japan and Climate Change, Japan and Cybersecurity</span></span></span></div>", "<span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\">Writing of final paper for the course - this may take several hours to complete depending on the students' ability to draft well in English. Submission deadline will be approximately 3 weeks after the last in-class session.</span></span>"], "第15回": ["<span style=\"font-size:13.28px;\"><span style=\"font-size:13.28px;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\">【Core Week 12】F </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:13.28px;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\">ace-to-face class -</span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:13.28px;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"> December 18, 2026 - 3rd period </span></span></span><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span style=\"font-size:13.28px;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\">《90 minutes》</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:13.28px;\"><strong style=\"font-size:9.545px;caret-color:rgb(38,40,42);color:rgb(38,40,42);font-family:Helvetica;\"><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></span><div><span style=\"font-size:13.28px;\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\">Course Conclusion:</span></span></span><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"> &nbsp;Review of The State of International Relations Today and Future Outlook</span></span></span><div style=\"font-size:13.28px;\"><span style=\"font-size:13.28px;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\">Final Discussion. &nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:13.28px;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\">Final Test.</span></span></span></div></div>", ""], "授業計画1": "<span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\">Typically, the sessions' topic will be introduced by the course lecturer in a 40-50 minute presentation followed by Q&amp;A, discussions and group work (mini-assignments in class or based on homework/readings in LUNA).</span></span><div><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\">At the beginning of each face-to-face class (core weeks 1-12), we will look at the past week's main international news/recent developments. This requires the students to follow the news on a daily basis in print/online media, or TV/radio.</span></span></div><div><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\">The \"flex hours\" segments of the course will be explained in class; there will be a 30-minute pre-recorded presentation and 60-minute self-study for the two sessions listed as \"flex hours\".&nbsp;</span></span></div>", "授業外学習2": "<span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\">Reading materials, homework assignments and any additional guidance will be shared with the students in class or through the LUNA system. Typically, students will need to spend 1-2 hours every week for reading and completing homework assignments not counting the flex-hour self-study.</span></span>"}, "評価": {"教科書/Required texts0": ["The books listed above will be held on reserve at the KGU library and/or the SIS library that is located on the second floor of the G Building. - Additional sources: o ther relevant articles and reading materials for this course will be provided in class for each session."], "教科書/Required texts1": ["Christian Reus-Smit", "International Relations: A Very Short Introduction", "Oxford University Press.", "2020 年", "9780198850212", ""], "教科書/Required texts2": ["Klaus Dodds", "Geopolitics: A Very Short Introduction", "Oxford University Press.", "2019 年", "9780198830764", ""], "教科書/Required texts3": ["Karen A. Mingst, Heather Elko McKibben, etc.", "Essentials of International Relations (8th Edition)", "W. W. Norton and the Company", "2021 年", "9780393872200", ""], "教科書/Required texts4": ["Joyce P. Kaufman", "Introduction to International Relations: Theory and Practice", "Rowman and Littlefield Publishers", "2022 年", "9781538158937", ""], "参考文献・資料/Reference books0": ["No additional titles listed here."], "学位授与の方針との関連Relationship to Diploma Policy0": 